## Context
Harness tickets 0375 and 1073 (ImperialDragonHarness PRs 1300 and 1309) moved
generalizable rules from this repo's `.claude/rules/` into the harness. Each
rule should now be stated once, at harness level. Source:
`~/.agents/docs/2026-10-09-t0375-project-rules-inventory.md` § Proposed trims.

## Actions
- `writing.md`: drop the absence-claim, one-paragraph-heading,
  no-in-repo-bibliography, gap-paragraph and inline-figure rules (now in harness
  `prose/_all.md`, `doctype/article.md` and `manuscript-build.md`). Shorten the
  hardcoded-crossref rule to the local test and house LaTeX conventions. Replace
  § CI test polarity rule with a pointer to harness `rules/prose-adherence-tests.md`,
  keeping the local anchor examples.
- `json-output.md`: delete (now in harness `rules/coding-python.md`). Keep the
  local test `test_json_eof_newline.py`.
- `workflow.md`: drop test-one-before-blasting and prefer-skills (now in harness
  `rules/authoring-skills.md`). Shorten § Derive prose from generated artifacts to
  the local test and the 0452 evidence.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Each listed rule is removed or reduced to a pointer; nothing aedist-specific is lost
- [ ] The local test suite passes
